class.description:
[method PCKPackageServer.build] copies the bytes of every source as it is. A description that lists [code]res://art/a.png[/code] then produces a pack with the PNG source, but without the [code].import[/code] file and the imported texture, so [code]load("res://art/a.png")[/code] fails in an exported game. [PCKPackageExporter] builds the same description with the export pipeline of an export preset instead:
- An entry whose source is a [code]res://[/code] file is packed in exported form for the preset's platform: its [code].import[/code] file and imported artifacts (for example [code].ctex[/code] textures in the formats of the platform), [code].remap[/code] files, scenes and resources converted to binary, and tokenized scripts. The preset's export plugins, script export mode, exclude filter and options (such as the shader baker) apply. The target path of such an entry must equal its source path, because the export keeps [code]res://[/code] paths; a renamed entry is refused.
- By default, the files these resources depend on are packed too, like in the "Export selected resources" mode. Files that belong to the main pack are never written: [code]project.binary[/code], the UID and global class caches, the GDExtension list, autoloads, icons, and the files that export plugins add for the whole project.
- Entries with data in memory, with a source outside [code]res://[/code] ([code]user://[/code] or an absolute path) and entries read from [member PCKPackage.base_pack] are copied as they are. They win over an exported file with the same path. Removal entries are written as removals.
- [code].import[/code], [code].remap[/code] and [code].uid[/code] entries with a [code]res://[/code] source are not needed: the export writes them for their source file. Listed without their source, they are refused.
- Files are encrypted with the preset's encryption settings and key (see [method should_encrypt]), and entries with their own [code]encrypt[/code] flag are encrypted too. Without a key in the preset, the key compiled into the engine is used. The directory is encrypted if the preset or [member PCKPackage.encrypted_directory] asks for it.
The pack is written only if every entry could be built. Errors are printed and returned as an [enum Error] value.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
@tool
extends EditorScript

func _run():
	var description := PCKPackage.new()
	description.add_file("scenes/level_2.tscn", "res://scenes/level_2.tscn")
	description.add_file("readme.txt", "user://dlc_readme.txt")
	var plan := PCKPackageExporter.plan_description(description)
	print(plan["export_sources"], plan["raw_files"], plan["errors"])
	var err := PCKPackageExporter.export_description(description, "Windows Desktop", "user://dlc.pck")
	if err != OK:
		push_error("Build failed: %s" % error_string(err))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
using Godot;

[Tool]
public partial class BuildDlc : EditorScript
{
	public override void _Run()
	{
		var description = new PckPackage();
		description.AddFile("scenes/level_2.tscn", "res://scenes/level_2.tscn");
		description.AddFile("readme.txt", "user://dlc_readme.txt");
		var plan = PckPackageExporter.PlanDescription(description);
		GD.Print(plan["export_sources"], plan["raw_files"], plan["errors"]);
		Error err = PckPackageExporter.ExportDescription(description, "Windows Desktop", "user://dlc.pck");
		if (err != Error.Ok)
		{
			GD.PushError($"Build failed: {err}");
		}
	}
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
The same build is available in the editor under [b]Project > Tools > Build Pack from Description...[/b] and on the command line:
[codeblock lang=text]
godot --headless --path <project> --export-pack-description "Windows Desktop" res://packs/dlc.tres builds/dlc.pck
[/codeblock]
The command waits for the first scan and import of the project, builds the pack in release mode and quits with exit code [code]0[/code], or [code]1[/code] if the build failed. A relative pack path is relative to the project folder.
The editor also registers an export plugin for packs. It keeps every file that is the export target of a preset out of new exports (for example [code]res://build/game.pck[/code], and the [code].pck[/code] next to an executable target), and warns when a preset encrypts a [code].pck[/code] file inside the main pack: such a pack is decrypted whole every time one of its files is opened. The export preset option [code]pck_packages/excluded_descriptions[/code] lists descriptions whose [code]res://[/code] sources are left out of the preset's normal exports, so content shipped as a separate pack is not in the main pack too.
[b]Note:[/b] This class is only available in editor builds and runs on the main thread. It cannot be instantiated: all methods are static.

method.description:
Returns how the entries of [param description] would be built, without building anything:
- [code]"export_sources"[/code]: a [PackedStringArray] of the [code]res://[/code] sources that go through the export pipeline;
- [code]"raw_files"[/code]: the pack paths that are copied as they are;
- [code]"removals"[/code]: the pack paths written as removal entries;
- [code]"skipped"[/code]: [code].import[/code], [code].remap[/code] and [code].uid[/code] entries that the export writes for their source anyway;
- [code]"errors"[/code]: one message per entry that can't be built, such as a renamed [code]res://[/code] target. Nothing is built while this array is not empty.
